*.ipynb linguist-detectable=false

# Hash-verified artifacts must check out byte-identically on every machine.
# A system-wide core.autocrlf=true would otherwise turn LF into CRLF on
# checkout, making baseline/upstream_sql_runner.py (and every manifest hash)
# mismatch the frozen SHA256.  This rule wins over user/global config.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Two upstream files ship with CRLF inside the commit archive; keep their
# bytes exactly as downloaded so the "unmodified upstream" claim stays true.
.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/*.md -text
